{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/675760-dragolescu-conversion","id":675760,"title":"Dragolescu Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T16:16:24-07:00","id":675760,"title":"Dragolescu Conversion","content":"I'm looking for a conversion of the Dragolescu bloodline. I've found one but it was grossly overpowered, and I just don't have the rules savvy to tinker it back to something more in line with the existing bloodline conversions out there. So I throw myself at your mercy.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help me create something for the devotion powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1554-vesper","name":"Vesper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T16:36:06-07:00","id":675791,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm..... form wodindex, our spread of powers is thus: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_wiki_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\"><b>Essentiaphagia</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\"><a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Bloodlines#Dragolescu\" target=\"_blank\">Dragolescu</a></td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Ordo p179</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Hunger for Essentia</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">(\u2022)</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">See ghosts and haunts</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Draw Ectoplasm</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">(\u2022\u2022)</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">-</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Gain Vitae and Willpower from ectoplasm</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Essentia Diffusion</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022)</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">EE or E\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Mimic ghost's numina</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Mnemophagia</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">EEEE\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Gain skill known by ghost in life</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_wiki_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Ghost Consumption</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">EEEEE\u25cb</td> <td class=\"text_table_wiki_table_td\">Merge with a ghost</td> </tr> </table></div> So, lets start, shall we? The first two are pretty basic. &quot;Detect ghosts and haunted houses.&quot; Pretty basic ability. I'd tie ectoplasm into the Location or Herd merit, no need to make it into a separate power. Rather, I'd make it part of the basic free ability all bloodlines start with. See ghosts/haunts. Feed from plasm. When combined with the rules from Book of the Dead on feeding from anchors, nothing too bad. In fact, the feeding on plasm is a requirement for the rest of the abilities, so lets just go ahead and say that all necessary abilities for further powers should be automatic. Merely seeing ghosts and feeding isn't mechanically broken.<br /> <br /> Now, this is where we start getting into broken area. Mimic Numina, gain free skills, and merge with ghosts. As well, a modern version of the rules likely will take into account the fact that ghosts have Influences now as well. Fortunately, we can limit the extent of abilities ghosts have by the simple fact that we're dealing with primarily rank 1 and 2 ghosts. I'm not really sure if we need to make a devotion out of this. There's no real equivalent. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd sooner design a merit (ala Keroberos) than devotions. Go all in with Ghost Consumption, and base it off of the Retainer/Mentor/Allies/Contact merits. You gain the skills and abilities of the ghost based on the Retainer merit (keeping it balanced), but unlike a social merit Retainer, this ghost is already inside your body and under your control. Its simple, it has precedent in game already (and thus, not broken), and reflects the abilities of Essentiaphagia without having to force things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}